        "text": "The current pace of U.S. infrastructure development is insufficient relative to strategic threats.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "National security depends on economic competitiveness and technological leadership.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Incremental policy changes are inadequate for addressing systemic challenges in infrastructure.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Elected leaders have a responsibility to respond to external competitive pressures.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 70759,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70759.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "This rightward drift we now know in New York, happened in Washington Heights, the West Bronx, Queens, which is where I grew up. It's working class communities of color. So how do you explain that? Is it all immigration? So what is that?",
