    "turn_idx": 90,
    "turn_text": "So you cannot have a system. where anyone anywhere can cross the border, declare asylum, and then remain here indefinitely. And there was a point at which the sheer number of people coming became overwhelming. Like it put unprecedented strain on the shelter system and social safety net of New York City. And I know Mayor Adams came under severe criticism for his, for excoriating the administration, but for me, the problem was not Mayor Adams complaining about the migrant crisis. The problem was the reality of the migrant crisis and the administration's failure to address it with the urgency that the public demanded. Look, I feel that we return to the center left on both immigration and public safety. Like, I'm cautious of the optimistic that communities of color will naturally gravitate toward the Democratic Party as it's natural home. That's my belief. We have to meet people where they are, or there's a limit to how far we can deviate from strongly held public sentiment on an issue like immigration.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_07",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "A system allowing anyone anywhere to cross the border, declare asylum, and remain indefinitely is unsustainable.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The real issue is the existence of the migrant crisis and the administration’s inadequate response.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The number of migrants arriving became so large that it overwhelmed New York City's shelter system and social safety net.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Public demand for urgent action on the migrant crisis was not being met by the administration.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Mayor Adams faced severe criticism for criticizing the federal administration regarding the migrant crisis.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "We should return to the center-left position on immigration and public safety.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
