    "turn_text": "This podcast is supported by The World as You'll Know It, a podcast about the forces shaping the future. Human beings are living longer than ever. Thanks to advances like vaccines, antibiotics, and clean water, we've added more than 30 years to the average lifespan in a little over a century. That's more than was added in the previous 10,000 years. More recently, huge progress has been made in treating deadly conditions like heart disease and cancer. Mortality rates for each have dropped by double digits. Now science is tackling a new challenge, curing aging itself. In this season of the world as you'll know it, host and science journalist Carl Zimmer speaks to some of the most respected scientists in the field of longevity research about what old age could look like in the future. Will new breakthroughs add even more years to our lives? Can older brains be rewired to function like younger ones? And which so-called biohacks actually work? The world as you'll know it, the future of aging, is available now.",
